.TH ciaaw_saw 3 "16 July 2026" "1.3.2" "Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
\"{{{
saw \- function
\"}}}

.SH LIBRARY
\"{{{
ciaaw library 
.RI ( libciaaw ", " \-lciaaw )
\"}}}

.SH SYNOPSIS
\"{{{ 
.IP Fortran 10
.BI "function saw(" s , ab , u )result(res)
.RS
.IP "" 3
.BI "character(len=*), intent(in) :: " s    
.IP "" 3
.BI "logical, intent(in), optional :: " ab 
.IP "" 3
.BI "logical, intent(in), optional :: " u  
.IP "" 3
.BI "real(dp) :: " res                      
.RE

.IP C 10
.BI "double ciaaw_saw(char *" s, "int " n, "bool " ab, "bool " u ");"

.IP Python 10
.BI "saw(" s: str, abridged: bool=True, uncertainty: bool=False)->float:
\"}}}

.SH DESCRIPTION
Get the standard atomic weight for the element \fIs\fP.
The default behavior is to provide the abridged value,\fIab is TRUE\fP, 
recommended by the CIAAW. 
The uncertainty can be retrieved by setting \fIu\fP=TRUE.

Arguments:
.IP \fIs\fP 10    
Element symbol.
.IP \fIab\fP 10 
Set to False if the abridged value is not desired. Default to TRUE.
.IP \fIu\fP 10
Set to True if the uncertainty is desired. Default to FALSE.


.SH RETURN VALUE
.IP NaN 10 
If the provided element is incorrect.
.IP -1 10  
If the element does not have a SAW.

.SH EXAMPLE
\"{{{
.PP
Fortran:
.nf
.ft CR
    use ciaaw
    saw("H", ab=.false., u=.true.)
.ft R
.fi

.PP
C:
.nf
.ft CR
    include <stdio.h>
    include "ciaaw.h"
    ciaaw_saw("H", 1, false, true)
.ft R
.fi

.PP
Python:
.nf
.ft CR
    import pyciaaw
    pyciaaw.saw("H", ab=False, u=True)
.ft R
.fi
\"}}}


.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ciaaw (3),
.BR ciaaw_cli (1),
.BR ciaaw_version (3),
.BR ciaaw_saw (3),
.BR ciaaw_ice (3),
.BR ciaaw_naw (3)
